'''Eek Airport''' {{airport codes|EEK<ref>[http://gc.kls2.com/airport/EEK EEK - Eek, Alaska]. Great Circle Mapper. Retrieved 2008-09-17.</ref>|PAEE<ref>{{SkyVector|PAEE}}. Retrieved 2008-09-17.</ref>|EEK}} is a state-owned public-use [[airport]] serving the city of [[Eek, Alaska|Eek]] in the [[Bethel Census Area, Alaska|Bethel Census Area]] of the [[U.S. state]] of [[Alaska]].<ref name=FAA-master-record />

As per [[Federal Aviation Administration]] records, this airport had 3,759 passenger boardings (enplanements) in [[calendar year]] 2007, an increase of 16% from the 3,241 enplanements in 2006.<ref name=FAA-2007-enplanements />

== Facilities ==
Eek Airport has one [[runway]] designated 17/35 with a 3,243 x 60&nbsp;ft (988 x 18 m) [[gravel]] surface.<ref name=FAA-master-record />

A federally funded project relocated the airport to a new location about two miles west of Eek.<ref>[http://notes5.state.ak.us/pn/pubnotic.nsf/53a2e6f2d0aafc648925672a00602f03/4796b0b55d33a94f89256bf10080aba2?OpenDocument Eek Airport Relocation, Stage 2] {{Webarchive|url=https://archive.today/20120713154336/http://notes5.state.ak.us/pn/pubnotic.nsf/53a2e6f2d0aafc648925672a00602f03/4796b0b55d33a94f89256bf10080aba2?OpenDocument |date=2012-07-13 }}. ''Online Public Notice''. State of Alaska. 2002-07-10.</ref><ref>[http://www.osborne.cc/past_civil.html Completed Projects: Eek Airport Relocation] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110706215620/http://www.osborne.cc/past_civil.html |date=2011-07-06 }}. Osborne Construction Company. Retrieved 2008-09-17.</ref> The former airport had a 1,400 by 35&nbsp;ft runway and was located east of Eek at coordinates {{coord|60|12.95|N|162|00.35|W|region:US_type:airport}}.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20050119184641/http://www.alaska.faa.gov/fai/images/ARPT_DIAGRAMS/EEK.gif Airport diagram] ([[GIF]]). Federal Aviation Administration, Alaskan Region. 2003-12-25.</ref>

